/-!
# Operator Möbius Peirce Algebra, Parabolic/Hyperbolic/Elliptic Rotors, Finite Corner Brackets,
# Modular Steinberg Relations, and 24-Periodic Cyclotomic Factorization in `[Ring B]`

Over an arbitrary associative ring `B` (`[Ring B]`), this module formalizes the noncommutative
operator identities of Orders 28–31 generated by an idempotent `P * P = P` and Peirce corners
`N_+ = P X (1 - P)`, `N_- = (1 - P) Y P`:

1. **Tetractys `𝔰𝔩₂(B)` Lie Algebra & Cartan Decomposition (`tetractys_is_sl2_moebius_lie_algebra`):**
   - **Lie Brackets:** `[S_P, Φ] = 2 • J`, `[S_P, J] = 2 • Φ`, `[J, Φ] = 2 • Σ` (`Σ = S_P * V`).
   - **Cartan Decomposition:** `J * J = -V`, `S_P * S_P = 1`, `Φ * Φ = V`, and
     `{S_P, Φ} = {S_P, J} = {Φ, J} = 0`.
   - **Central Metric & Casimir:** `[V, S_P] = [V, Φ] = [V, J] = 0` and
     `S_P * S_P * V + Φ * Φ - J * J = 3 • V`.
2. **Root Space & Parabolic Horocycle Flows (`root_space_and_parabolic_horocycle_flow`):**
   - `[S_P, N_+] = 2 • N_+`, `[S_P, N_-] = -(2 • N_-)`, `[N_+, N_-] = Σ`, `{N_+, N_-} = V`.
   - Unipotent shears `parabolicFlowPlus P X t = 1 + t * N_+` and
     `parabolicFlowMinus P Y t = 1 + t * N_-` obey `(1 + t N_±)(1 + s N_±) = 1 + (t + s) N_±`
     for central `t, s : B`.
3. **Hyperbolic Weyl Dilation & Elliptic Rotors (`hyperbolic_weyl_dilation_action`,
   `elliptic_rotation_casimir_and_bruhat_moebius_orbit`):**
   - `(1 + S_P) N_+ (1 - S_P) = 4 • N_+`, `(1 - S_P) N_- (1 + S_P) = 4 • N_-`, and polynomial
     rotor conjugations `(c + s S_P) N_± (c - s S_P) = (c ± s)² N_±` for central `c, s : B`.
   - Elliptic norm-square `(c + s J)(c - s J) = c² + s² V` and degree-3 Bruhat–Möbius projector
     closure `G_+ P G_+⁻¹ = P + Φ - Σ - V N_+`.
4. **Finite Peirce Corner Bracket Relations:**
   - The grading element acts on the opposite Peirce corners with weights `+2` and `-2`, and their
     commutator is `Σ = S_P * V = V * S_P`. These identities alone do not define a mode algebra.
5. **Universal Modular Steinberg Defect & Unit-Metric `SL(2)` Presentation in `[Ring B]`:**
   - For `S = N_- - N_+ = -J`, `T_+ = 1 + N_+`, and `T_- = 1 - N_-`, every `[Ring B]` satisfies
     `T_+ T_- T_+ = J + (1 - V) T_+` and `T_- T_+ T_- = J + (1 - V) T_-`; when `V = 1`,
     `S² = -1`, `S⁴ = 1`, `(S T_+)² = S T_+ - 1`, `(S T_+)³ = -1 = S²`, and `(S T_+)⁶ = 1`.
6. **Centralizer Collapse, 4-Way Linear Diamond of `1 - J⁴`, & Cyclotomic Operator Identity:**
   - Any `c : B` commuting with `P` annihilates `J`, `Φ`, `V`, `Σ`, whereas for general `X, Y : B`,
     `(1 - J)(1 + J)(1 - Φ)(1 + Φ) = 1 - J⁴` and
     `(1 - J)(1 + J)(1 - Φ)(1 + Φ)(1 + J⁴ + J⁸)(1 + J⁴) Φ₂₄(J) = 1 - J²⁴` inside `B`.

